# Cloud — our control-plane dashboard, as a workbook

Our cloud dashboard (formerly `web/cloud-dashboard`, a SvelteKit app) migrated to a **`.work`
workbook**: one `client` island that IS the dashboard SPA. The Svelte components were ported
**verbatim** — every `<style>` copied byte-for-byte (the theme is exact) and every component's DOM
reproduced exactly — into a vanilla island the nexus renders (no SvelteKit, no build step). The shell
is the sidebar + topbar; the views (Nexus overview, Usage, Storage, Database, Team, Secrets, Settings,
Upgrade, Sharing, Workspace, nexus detail, plus the bare Welcome/Authorize/Denied) are reproduced
one-for-one.

**Auth seam.** The island authenticates to the control plane (`/api/platform`) with our OWN native
session cookie (`Nexus.Auth.Session`, set by `/auth/login`). No session ⇒ the platform API answers
401 and the island bounces to `/login/`. The `work` CLI uses a `wbk_` PAT on the same `/api/platform`
— one auth path for browser and CLI; nothing about auth is baked into the runtime.

## The data — dogfooded straight off the platform

The dashboard reads the platform's own primitives via `/api/platform/*` (the hosted control plane,
`Nexus.Platform`). This `server` block additionally exposes `usage`/`fleet`/`storage` live sources
backed by `Nexus.Capacity` for the dogfood nexus serving it, and mints real CLI tokens.

resource Event do
  description "The activity feed — every bus #event the dashboard persists (who did what, where, when)."
  tags ["system", "activity"]
  kind :string
  actor :string
  title :string
  target :string
  tags :string
  scope :string
  at :integer
end

# A durable agent-run record — one row per agent run (tenant-scoped SQLite). Written when a run
# finishes (streamed live over the `agent_run` Live source); read back by the Studio Runs view.
resource Run do
  description "Agent run history — one row per agent run (who launched it, the brief, status, tokens)."
  tags ["system", "agents"]
  rid :string       # run id (stable handle, distinct from the storage row id)
  agent :string     # which named agent ran
  user :string      # who launched it
  task :string      # the brief
  status :string    # ok | error | timeout
  turns :integer    # LLM turns taken
  tokens :integer   # total tokens (from telemetry)
  answer :string    # final answer (truncated for the list view)
  started :integer  # unix seconds
  ended :integer    # unix seconds
end

# The task/plan store — the orchestration backbone. A task is a unit of work; a plan is a parent
# task with child subtasks (parent = parent's tid). Dispatching a task launches a Run and links its
# rid. THE LINE: the bus + `task` effect are generic; this store + the Studio board are our cloud.
resource Todo do
  description "The task & issue board — units of work and filed problems the orchestration dispatches."
  tags ["system", "orchestration"]
  tid :string        # stable task id
  kind :string       # "task" (work to do) | "issue" (a problem an agent/human filed) — one fabric
  title :string      # short summary
  detail :string     # the brief / acceptance (for an issue: the failure context + proposed fix)
  status :string     # open | in_progress | blocked | done | cancelled
  agent :string      # assignee (a named agent), or "" if unassigned
  parent :string     # parent task tid for plan decomposition, or "" for a root task
  priority :integer  # 0 (top) .. 4 (backlog)
  created_by :string # who/what filed it (a user, or an agent name)
  run :string        # the rid of the dispatched run (a task) or the FAILING run (an issue)
  created :integer   # unix seconds
  updated :integer   # unix seconds
end

# Scheduled agent runs — the time arm of the orchestration fabric. A schedule fires a named agent on a
# brief via Nexus.Scheduler (the durable OTP scheduler, same fire path as hook triggers). Append-only,
# folded by sid (latest wins) like Todo; re-armed on boot. THE LINE: the scheduler is the open standard;
# persisting + managing these schedules is our cloud product.
resource Schedule do
  description "Scheduled agent runs — the time arm of orchestration (cron/every/at), re-armed on boot."
  tags ["system", "orchestration"]
  sid :string        # stable schedule id
  agent :string      # the named agent to run
  task :string       # the brief
  mode :string       # every | cron | at | after
  spec :string       # the value for the mode: "15m" | "0 9 * * 1" | "14:00"
  owner :string      # who created it
  created :integer   # unix seconds
  enabled :integer   # 1 armed, 0 cancelled
end

# Persist every bus event to the log. The reactive primitives (hook kind, #event, effect engine) are
# the open standard; this hook + the `log` effect are our cloud opting into a durable feed.
hook :activity do
  match tags: [:event]
  log
end

